{
  "_note": "Harvestable resource nodes and the tools that work them, modelled on Deep Rock Galactic: Survivor. Mining there is the primary XP source in the early game \u2014 you climb the first few levels off the rock, not the kills \u2014 and that is the job this table does. Everything is content: HP, payouts, spawn weights and tool speeds all live here.",
  "_harvestNote": "Harvesting is PROXIMITY-BASED and continuous, not a weapon hit. Stand near a node and the tool works on its own, so mining never competes with a weapon slot and never asks the player to stop shooting. That is also why the tools are not in weapons.json: everyone starts with both, and they upgrade on their own ladder.",
  "_tierNote": "Six tiers, named for the Pixcuit icon pack's materials so every tier has real art. The ladder was five (wood/stone/iron/steel/diamond) before the art arrived; matching the pack beat inventing a steel-to-titanium mapping.",
